7. ARM vs General-Purpose Processors 

	Feature 		ARM 			General Purpose CPU

	Power consumption	low 	 		High
	Instruction set 	RISC 			Often CISC 
	Application 		Embedded, Mobile	PCs, Servers
	Heat generation		Low 			High

8. Key Advantages of ARM Architecture 

	* Low power consumption
	* High performance per watt
	* Compact instruction set
	* Scalable architecture 
	* Suitable for real-time systems	

9. Summary 

	* ARM is a RISC based processor architecture.
	* It uses load-store design, fixed instruction length, and pipelining
	* ARM is widely used in SoC-based embedded systems.
	* Its low power consumption makes it ideal for mobile and embedded applications.






















 























































































